writes; gold_set, scorers, and coverage_threshold are never mentioned in the plan text"],"finding":"The plan claims every written .eval.yaml passes validate_eval_spec(strict=True) with zero errors, but never specifies the mandatory sibling fields of the eval-spec schema the runner must emit — strict validation requires a non-empty gold_set plus epochs, an at_least(k) gate, a coverage_threshold, and a non-empty scorers list with ≥1 deterministic scorer, none of which the admission runner is said to write.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc004ce3603c4c801","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Disposition ('written to .rebar/evals/<prompt-id>.eval.yaml only when its reproducing cases still form a balanced ... dataset validate_eval_spec(strict=True) accepts'); Acceptance Criteria line 'Every written spec returns zero errors from validate_eval_spec(spec, strict=True)'","norm_id":"nc683a16caf7ff6bb","priority":0.2085,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The admission runner writes a spec containing only prompt + dataset; validate_eval_spec(strict=True) returns errors for missing gold_set/scorers/epochs/gate/coverage_threshold, so no criterion can ever be admitted and AC #4 fails on the first written file","A reviewer or executor cannot tell whether the gold_set is copied from the mined candidate, synthesized, or reused from a packaged built-in — the provenance of the judge-alignment gold_set is undefined"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the runner emits, alongside the reproducing dataset, a fixed spec skeleton (epochs: 3, gate: at_least(2), coverage_threshold, and the deterministic criterion scorer) and derives a non-empty balanced gold_set (e.g. from the reproducing must-fire/must-not-fire case inputs and their observed labels), then name that skeleton as the thing validate_eval_spec(strict=True) accepts.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","as